 <P STYLE="margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"><FONT STYLE="font-family:Times New Roman" SIZE="2"><B>Alternative Minimum Tax </B></FONT></P>
<P STYLE="margin-top:6px;margin-bottom:0px; text-indent:4%"><FONT STYLE="font-family:Times New Roman" SIZE="2">With limited exceptions, taxpayers must pay an alternative minimum tax if it exceeds the taxpayer&#146;s regular federal income tax for
the year. For noncorporate taxpayers, the alternative minimum tax is imposed on alternative minimum taxable income, or AMTI, that is above an exemption amount. AMTI generally is taxable income, plus or minus various adjustments, plus tax preference
items. </FONT></P> <P STYLE="margin-top:12px;margin-bottom:0px; text-indent:4%"><FONT STYLE="font-family:Times New Roman" SIZE="2">Some of the principal adjustments to taxable income that are used to determine AMTI are summarized below. </FONT></P>
