Code section does not deal expressly with respect to the treatment of members of limited liability companies for purposes of the self-employment tax. In 1997, the IRS promulgated proposed regulations to define when a partner in a partnership or
member of a limited liability company should be considered to be a limited partner for purposes of this exclusion from the self-employment tax. Under those proposed regulations, members who do not have personal liability for limited liability
company debts, the authority under the laws of the state of formation to contract on behalf of the limited liability company, or otherwise do not participate in its activities would not be subject to the self-employment tax. However, the proposed
